e are of the ClearType Font Collection, a suite of fonts from various designers released with Windows Vista. All start with the letter C to reflect that they were designed to work well with Microsoft's ClearType text rendering system, a text rendering engine designed to make text clearer to read on LCD monitors.", "role": "answer_reveal", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2025-12-11T16:27:48Z", "username": "Kartikey Pradhan", "text": "However, Meiryo doesn’t start with C, still makes it to the list. How?", "role": "elaboration", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2025-12-11T16:28:18Z", "username": "Dhruv", "text": "Is it spelled like that in Japanese", "role": "attempt", "is_correct": true, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2025-12-11T16:28:39Z", "username": "Kartikey Pradhan", "text": "I will give it to you. Meiryo in Japanese means “clarity”", "role": "elaboration", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2025-12-11T16:29:08Z", "username": "మాన$", "text": "They do not have tails. Sans serif", "role": "elaboration", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}]